! The hole ender of `phrasing.xfst`: the verb of the clause is the word written
! next, so the clause is stroked first and the word after it.
!
! Its own directory, and not part of `tests/golden/phrasing.tsv`, because what a
! golden file asks is what one outline means and what these ask is what two of
! them write together. The inflection is `{:infl:…}`, a lexicon, so this needs
! `build/morph` and `check.sh` skips it where those are absent.
!
! `scripts/check-hold.py` replays every case here through a real Plover engine
! and compares, so each line is two hosts' answer.

! ---- the verb hole, `-RG`, over the corners of the clause
!buffer
+T-RG
RUPB
!buffer
+T-RGD
RUPB
!buffer
+TERG
RUPB
!buffer
+TURG
RUPB

! A modal takes the base form, so the hole asks for nothing at all and the word
! stands as it was written.
!buffer
+TARG
RUPB

! The passive, the negative and the question, which are the same corners a verb
! of its own would take.
!buffer
+PH-RG
RUPB
!buffer
+K*RG
RUPB
!buffer
#+T-RG
RUPB

! An irregular, which is why the tail is a lexicon and not a rule.
!buffer
+T-RGD
TKPW
!buffer
+TURG
TKPW

! ---- a held clause, `🦐`: it waits before its verb for the next stroke
! The gap sits after the finite word, so the stroke lands where an adverb goes,
! and whatever it writes lands there: a stroke, not a word.
!buffer
🦐+K-R
^OEFPB
!buffer
🦐+KUR
^TPH-FR
!buffer
🦐+K*R
AULS
!buffer
🦐#+T-R
^OEFPB
!buffer
🦐+HR-R
^RAUL
!buffer
🦐+PH-B
^OEFPB
!buffer
🦐+K-FPTS
^RAUL

! With nothing after the gap there is no tail, so the stroke just follows.
!buffer
🦐+K
^OEFPB

! ---- what the hole displaced
!buffer
+T-RGT
!buffer
+T-RPGT
!buffer
+T-RGTZ

! ---- the other hole: a determiner subject holds the noun
! The clause after the determiner is the tail, so the noun lands in the middle
! of it. `S` pluralizes and the agreement follows the determiner, not the noun.
!buffer
+PR-B
KAT
!buffer
+SPR-B
KATS
!buffer
+KP-B
KAT

! Question inversion needs nothing of its own: the subject is still followed by
! the space the finite word left.
!buffer
#+PR-B
KAT

! A hole with nothing after it holds nothing, because there is no tail to wait
! with, so the noun follows as ordinary text.
!buffer
#+PR
KAT

! ---- the question tag, `#^`: a clause with no verb waits for its complement
!buffer
#^+T
TPHAOEUS
!buffer
#^+K
HRAEUT
!buffer
#^+K-GZ
SKAOL
!buffer
#^+T-B
